hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"23609","Sufyan narrated to us, Mansur narrated to me from his maternal uncle Musafi' from Safiyyah bint Shaybah mother of Mansur, she said: A woman from Banu Sulaym who delivered most of the people of our house informed me: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent to Uthman ibn Talhah, and once he said: She asked Uthman: Why did the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, call you? He said: I had seen the two horns of the ram when I entered the House, and I forgot to order you to cover them, so cover them, for there should not be in the House anything that preoccupies the one who prays. Sufyan said: The two horns of the ram remained in the House until the House burned and they burned. This is the end of the hadith."
